{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, קַדְמָה","hw":"קַדְמָה","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">קַדְמָה</span>]</big>  <strong>n.f. former time (</strong>cf. BH <a data-ref=\"BDB, קַדְמָה\" href=\"/BDB,_קַדְמָה\", dir=\"rtl\">קַדְמָה</a>, Zinj. <span dir=\"rtl\">קדמה</span> (Cooke<sup>177</sup>), <em>former state</em><strong>)</strong>;—cstr. <a data-ref=\"Daniel 6:11\" href=\"/Daniel.6.11\">Dn 6:11</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן־קַדְמַת דְּנָה</span> = <em>before this, formerly;</em> so <a data-ref=\"Ezra 5:11\" href=\"/Ezra.5.11\">Ezr 5:11</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מִקַּדְמַת דְּ׳</span>. cf. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 28:19\" href=\"/Genesis.28.19\">Gn 28:19</a> 𝔗<sup>J</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 38:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.38.17\">Ez 38:17</a> 𝔗.","next":"BDB Aramaic, קַדְמָי","prev":"BDB Aramaic, קֳדָם"}